    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe request may now include an optional `birthDate` (ISO date). When present, the owner's response carries `ageBand`, computed by measuring age against the owner's `registrationDate`: `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+). Absent when no `birthDate` was supplied.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (format `date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs are generated from this at build time.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, column `birth_date`) with accessors, so it survives the create\u2192GET round-trip. MapStruct maps it in automatically by name.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`mapper/AgeBands.java`** (new) \u2014 helper that derives the band from `birthDate` vs `registrationDate` (using `ChronoUnit.YEARS`), returning `null` when no birth date is set so the field is omitted.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `ageBand` via a mapping expression, consistent with the other derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.).\n\nThis follows the existing \"derived on read\" pattern (helper class + MapStruct expression), keeping the OfficeFloor pipeline untouched \u2014 no new function steps were needed since the band is computed in the response mapping rather than stored.\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, BUILD SUCCESS.",
